# Studify Environment Configuration

# Where the Studify API lives, including /api (Optional)
# Leave empty in development: the dev server proxies /api to http://localhost:3001.
# For a deployed site: e.g. https://api.example.com/api (the API's ALLOWED_ORIGINS must list the site).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Google Identity Services OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Optional)
# If left empty, Studify automatically provides local student profiles on this device.
# For production Google Sign-In, create a Web Client ID in the Google Cloud Console:
# https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# Authorized JavaScript Origins: http://localhost:5173 (and your production domain)
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Note: Gemini AI API Key is configured securely by each user within the app UI (Settings -> Gemini API Key)
# and saved in the user's browser localStorage. Never commit API keys to client-side bundles.
